From 7850e1bacf85a69b0d239c4e64519ad4f6ed0d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:15:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: card icons say the card's state, and the tasks pill
 says it opens
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo proposal §6.67, asks 90 and 93 (2026-11-22).

Conversation cards. 0125 gave tool, terminal and edit cards three states
-- collapsed (one line), minimized (the whole command or title) and
maximized (with the content) -- but kept upstream's single Disclosure:
ChevronDown while collapsed and while minimized, ChevronUp maximized, so a
card's state could not be read from its icon, and the same ChevronDown is
the tasks card's "Move to Bottom". The header now draws the state's own
buttons, the pinned card's pair (ExpandVertical, and FoldVertical, its
inside-out) with a chevron for the content between them:

  collapsed   ExpandVertical -> minimized
  minimized   ChevronDown -> maximized, then FoldVertical -> collapsed
  maximized   ChevronUp -> minimized, then FoldVertical -> collapsed

The fold sits at the end, where the expand button sat while collapsed. A
card with nothing to maximize offers only the fold. The rule is
tool_card_display::header_controls, a pure function, and the steps are no
longer a ring: maximized goes back to minimized, and collapsing is the
fold's. It replaces next_display and ThreadView::step_tool_card, which
only the chevron used; ThreadView::set_tool_card moves a card to the
button's target, and render_tool_card_controls draws the buttons for both
the terminal card (TerminalToolHeader::controls takes the place of its
Disclosure, which stays only for the component preview, now without a
click handler: on_toggle_expand had no caller left) and the generic and
edit cards. They show on hover of the card's header, as the chevron did;
the buttons hide, not their boxes, because a hidden element paints no
children. Two-state cards (subagent, thinking) keep their chevrons. An
Execute card without terminal content still has no toggle; out of scope.

Tasks card. Minimized, its pill (0037, 0080, 0092) showed only an icon and
a count, while its tooltip said "Expand Tasks Card". It now ends in a
Maximize icon, the inverse of the Minimize that made it; the whole pill
stays the click target.

Tests:
- tool_card_display::tests: each_state_shows_its_own_buttons,
  a_card_without_content_has_no_chevron (new), and the step test, through
  the primary button's target, is now
  a_click_steps_up_to_maximized_and_back_to_minimized. Red seen against
  the old single chevron.
- conversation_view::tests::tool_card_display_tests: the three-state test
  steps maximized back to minimized and folds with set_tool_card;
  the_header_draws_the_buttons_of_its_state (new, by debug bounds). Red
  seen.
- tasks_card::pill_expand (new): the icon trails the count inside the
  pill, and a click on it opens the card. Red seen: "the pill shows an
  expand icon".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
